27:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"addresses"}]," is the only required field. The URL carries everything Redis needs:\nscheme, optional credentials, host, port and database index.\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"redis://username:password@redis-server-url:6380/99"}]," selects port 6380 and\ndatabase 99. Keep credentials out of the file by writing\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"redis://${REDIS_USER}:${REDIS_PASSWORD}@redis:6379/"}]," and exporting the\nvariables; see ",["$","$L1b",null,{"href":"/configuration/config-file","children":"The config file"}],"."]}]
